title: Bump ark-vrf to 0.6.1
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Bumps `ark-vrf` from 0.5.3 to 0.6.1. The Bandersnatch VRF primitives in `sp-core` use the new
    API and its stricter decoders:

    - All points and proofs decode with the `_exact` decoders, which reject trailing bytes.
    - The decoder of `RingVerifierKey` now checks the curve points. A key with a point out of the
      prime-order subgroup does not decode.
    - Ring member keys decode with the subgroup and identity checks. A key that fails the checks
      takes the slot of the padding point. Before, an identity key made `RingContext::prover` and
      `RingContext::verifier_key` panic.
    - The decoder of `RingContext` does not check the points, because the SRS comes from a
      trusted setup.

    The public `sp-core` traits `VrfSecret` and `VrfPublic` do not change. The ring VRF tickets of
    the `pallet-sassafras` tests, made with `ark-vrf` 0.5.0, still verify.
crates:
- name: sp-core
  bump: minor
